<p class="lh"><strong>FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE</strong> &nbsp;|&nbsp; January 10, 2025</p>

<p class="lh"><strong>Global Partnership Announcement:</strong> SanguineIT today announced a strategic partnership with a leading cloud alliance to strengthen enterprise modernization programs across North America, Europe, and APAC delivery markets. The collaboration expands SanguineIT’s ability to support large-scale migration, platform engineering, FinOps governance, and managed operations for organizations navigating complex multi-cloud and hybrid transformation agendas.</p>

<h2>Strategic focus of the alliance</h2>
<p class="lh">The partnership is designed to address a common challenge in enterprise cloud adoption: organizations can define modern architecture targets, but often struggle to execute at speed while maintaining security, compliance, and cost discipline. Through this alliance, SanguineIT combines its delivery management model with certified cloud capabilities, reference architecture assets, and deeper regional execution capacity for high-priority transformation programs.</p>

<p class="lh">Joint initiatives will focus on modernization outcomes that can be measured in both technical and business terms, including reduced migration risk, faster release velocity, improved reliability, and stronger unit-economics visibility for infrastructure spend. The program also supports organizations transitioning from project-based cloud activity to operating-model maturity with platform teams and continuous optimization practices.</p>

<h2>What clients can expect</h2>
<p class="lh">As part of the alliance, SanguineIT will deliver integrated service tracks that align architecture planning with execution and operational governance. The emphasis is on practical acceleration rather than one-size-fits-all migration mandates.</p>

<ul class="news-article-list">
    <li>Cloud landing zone design with policy controls, identity standards, and compliance-ready guardrails.</li>
    <li>Application portfolio assessments with phased migration blueprints and risk-prioritized sequencing.</li>
    <li>Platform engineering for containers, Kubernetes operations, and automated delivery pipelines.</li>
    <li>FinOps frameworks covering cost allocation, anomaly monitoring, and executive spend governance.</li>
    <li>Managed reliability services with observability, incident response, and continuous performance tuning.</li>
</ul>

<p class="lh">This structure allows enterprise technology leaders to engage a single accountable partner for cross-functional execution while still leveraging alliance capabilities where additional scale, certification depth, or regional support coverage is needed.</p>

<h2>Business outcomes and market relevance</h2>
<p class="lh">Global enterprises increasingly require cloud programs that balance speed with governance. Boards and executive leadership teams are demanding clearer evidence of modernization value, not just infrastructure migration activity. By combining strategic advisory with delivery execution and managed operations, SanguineIT and its cloud alliance partner aim to reduce transformation friction and accelerate measurable value realization.</p>

<p class="lh">For organizations modernizing legacy estates, this partnership can shorten the path from assessment to production workloads, while preserving strong controls around security posture, financial accountability, and service continuity. It is particularly relevant for businesses managing regulated data, high-volume customer systems, or mission-critical internal platforms.</p>

<p class="lh">The alliance also supports organizations operating across diverse regulatory jurisdictions by combining standardized governance frameworks with region-aware execution practices. This balance helps enterprises scale cloud programs internationally while preserving local compliance alignment, operational resilience, and transparent accountability to business leadership.</p>

<p class="lh">Program teams can also benefit from faster access to specialized expertise during critical migration and optimization windows.</p>

